 "article": {
  "title": "The Quiet Power of the Public Library",
  "topic": "文化（公共图书馆）",
  "level": "CET-4",
  "words": 320,
  "paras": [
   "In an age when almost any book can be found on a phone, some people wonder whether public libraries still matter. A visit to almost any town library answers the question. Libraries are a standard feature of the modern city, yet every one of them is different. On a rainy Tuesday morning, the reading room is full: a student prepares for an exam, an old man reads the newspaper, and a mother helps her child choose a picture book. The library is quiet, but it is never empty.",
   "What makes a library special is not only the books on its shelves. It offers something that money cannot easily buy: a warm, safe and free space that belongs to everyone. There is no need to buy a coffee or pass a security check. Anyone may sit, read, think or simply rest for a while. For those who live alone or work from home, that space can be a lifeline. Studies even suggest that reading for pleasure lowers stress and improves memory, so an hour in the library may do more good than an hour of scrolling on a phone.",
   "Libraries have also changed with the times. Many now lend tools, run free classes and help people fill in official forms online. Some offer language lessons for newcomers and quiet rooms for people working at a distance. In this way, a building that once stored books has become a valuable part of community life. Its worth is measured not by how many books it holds, but by how many lives it touches.",
   "Of course, libraries face real problems: tight budgets, fewer staff and the challenge of staying relevant. Yet cutting them to save money is often a false economy. A library is more than a shelf of books; it is a promise that knowledge and quiet belong to all of us. In a noisy, busy world, that promise is worth keeping."
  ],
  "zh": "在几乎任何书都能在手机上找到的时代，有人怀疑公共图书馆是否还有意义。可走进任何一座城镇图书馆，答案就摆在眼前。图书馆的意义不只在书架上的书，更在于它提供了一个温暖、安全、免费、属于所有人的空间：不必消费，也无需安检，谁都能进来坐一坐。对独居或居家办公的人来说，这里甚至是一条“救命绳”；研究还表明，为兴趣而读书能减压、增强记忆。图书馆也在与时俱进：出借工具、开设免费课程、帮人填写线上表格，成了社区生活的一部分。当然，它也面临预算紧张等现实困难，但为省钱而砍掉图书馆往往得不偿失——它是一份“知识与安静属于每个人”的承诺，值得守护。",
  "hard": [
